      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-63069",
      ":question/problem": "The heights of the players of two volleyball teams, Team $A$ and Team $B$, are recorded. The heights of Team $A$'s players have an interquartile range (IQR) of $0.3ft$. The heights of Team $B$'s players are given below:\n$5.1ft, 5.7ft, 5.9ft, 6ft, 6.1ft, 6.2ft, 6.3ft$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The heights of Team $B$'s players have an IQR of $0.3ft$.\n2. The IQR for Team $A$ is smaller than for Team $B$.\n3. A comparison of the IQRs suggests more variation in Team $A$'s players' heights.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
